              "description": "Represents the type of network access and/or any applicable authorization status the client is using. - **Wired clients** may have direct access without additional authorization. - **Wireless clients** can be connected via a protected network or an open network that may require additional authorization (e.g., a guest portal). - **VPN clients** may have different authorization mechanisms. Currently, the only two supported access types are `GUEST` (used for wired and wireless guest clients) and `DEFAULT` (a placeholder, which might be refined in the future releases, used for all other clients). Filtering is possible by `access.type`, for example `access.type.eq('GUEST')` to list guest clients.",
